IMPORT prelude

-- Legal Profession Act 1966 (Singapore) -- what a client and a non-lawyer meet: who may practise and the unauthorised-
-- practice offences (ss 32 to 36), the arbitration and mediation carve-outs (ss 35, 35B), the ban on no-win-no-fee
-- (s 107) and its conditional-fee exception (s 115B), suing for fees and assessing a bill (ss 118, 122), and the grounds
-- and sanctions for discipline (s 83).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/ (amendments to
-- Act 37 of 2023).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 36 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository, mostly s 2 (22). SCOPED from 636,000
-- characters to the provisions a client or a non-lawyer service provider meets. Not encoded: the Director of Legal
-- Services, the Institute, admission, practising certificates, foreign lawyers and the SICC, law practice entities,
-- accounts, unclaimed client money, the disciplinary machinery beyond s 83, remuneration orders, and most of Part 9.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Legal Profession Act 1966 -- clients and non-lawyers`

§§ `32 -- who is unauthorised`

-- s 32(1), (2): an "unauthorised person" is anyone who is not (a) on the roll of advocates and solicitors WITH a practising
-- certificate in force, or (b) on the roll of lawyers (NP) with a provisional practising certificate, acting under a
-- solicitor's supervision.
DECLARE Practitioner HAS
    `on the roll of advocates and solicitors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a practising certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on the roll of lawyers (NP) with a provisional certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `supervised by a solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the person` IS A Practitioner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is an unauthorised person` IF
    NOT (    (`the person`'s `on the roll of advocates and solicitors` AND `the person`'s `holds a practising certificate`)
         OR  (`the person`'s `on the roll of lawyers (NP) with a provisional certificate` AND `the person`'s `supervised by a solicitor`))

§§ `33, 34, 35, 35B -- what an unauthorised person may not do`

-- s 33(2): an unauthorised person who "directly or indirectly -- (a) draws or prepares any document or instrument relating
-- to any movable or immovable property or to any legal proceeding; (b) takes instructions for or draws or prepares any
-- papers on which to found or oppose a grant of probate ...; (d) on behalf of a claimant ... writes, publishes or sends a
-- letter or notice THREATENING LEGAL PROCEEDINGS other than a letter or notice that the matter will be handed to a
-- solicitor ...; or (e) ... negotiates ... the settlement of ... any claim arising out of personal injury or death" commits an
-- offence "UNLESS he or she proves that the act was not done for or in expectation of any fee, gain or reward". (5): first
-- offence $10,000; then $25,000 or 6 months.
-- s 33(10): "In this section, 'document' and 'instrument' DO NOT INCLUDE -- (a) A WILL or other testamentary document".
-- s 34(1): exceptions include (e) a person acting for themselves; (i) an accountant drawing documents in the exercise of
-- the profession; (f) an insurer's full-time employee settling an insured personal injury claim.
-- s 35: ss 32 and 33 do not extend to (b) "any person representing any party in arbitration proceedings" or (c) advice,
-- documents and assistance in them, "except for the right of audience in court proceedings".
-- s 35B: nor to certified mediators, mediators under a designated provider, and some foreign lawyers in mediation.
--
-- A will-writing service may charge to draft a will; a property agent who charges to draft a tenancy agreement commits an
-- offence. A debt collector's demand letter threatening legal action, sent for a fee, is an offence -- unless it says only
-- that the matter will be handed to a solicitor. And anyone, lawyer or not, may represent a party in an arbitration
-- seated in Singapore.
DECLARE Task IS ONE OF
    `drafting a will`
    `drafting a tenancy agreement`
    `drafting a sale and purchase agreement`
    `preparing probate papers`
    `a demand letter threatening legal proceedings`
    `a letter saying the matter will go to a solicitor`
    `negotiating a personal injury settlement`
    `representing a party in an arbitration`
    `representing a party in court`
    `conducting a certified mediation`

DECLARE TaskFacts HAS
    `the task` IS A Task
    `done for a fee, gain or reward` IS A BOOLEAN
    `acting for oneself` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an accountant in the exercise of the profession` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A TaskFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the unauthorised person commits an offence` IF
        NOT `the facts`'s `acting for oneself`
    AND CONSIDER `the facts`'s `the task`
        WHEN `drafting a will` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a letter saying the matter will go to a solicitor` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `representing a party in an arbitration` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `conducting a certified mediation` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `representing a party in court` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `drafting a tenancy agreement` THEN `the facts`'s `done for a fee, gain or reward` AND NOT `the facts`'s `an accountant in the exercise of the profession`
        WHEN `drafting a sale and purchase agreement` THEN `the facts`'s `done for a fee, gain or reward` AND NOT `the facts`'s `an accountant in the exercise of the profession`
        OTHERWISE `the facts`'s `done for a fee, gain or reward`

-- The burden: the unauthorised person must prove the absence of a fee (s 33(2)).
GIVEN `the facts` IS A TaskFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the defendant bears the burden of proving no fee` IF
    CONSIDER `the facts`'s `the task`
    WHEN `drafting a tenancy agreement` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `drafting a sale and purchase agreement` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `preparing probate papers` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a demand letter threatening legal proceedings` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `negotiating a personal injury settlement` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `36 -- fees paid to an unauthorised person`

-- s 36(1): "No costs in respect of anything done by an unauthorised person as an advocate or a solicitor ... are
-- recoverable". (2): "Any payment to an unauthorised person for anything done ... which is an offence under section 33 may
-- be recovered by the person who paid the money".
GIVEN `the act was an offence under section 33` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the client may recover what was paid` IF
    `the act was an offence under section 33`

§§ `107, 115B -- no-win-no-fee`

-- s 107(1)(b): a solicitor must not enter into an agreement to conduct contentious proceedings "which stipulates for or
-- contemplates payment ONLY IN THE EVENT OF SUCCESS". (3): solicitors are subject to the law of maintenance and champerty.
-- (3AA): except a conditional fee agreement complying with Part 8A.
-- s 115B(1): a conditional fee agreement may be made "in PRESCRIBED proceedings" only. (4): it must be "(a) in writing and
-- signed by the client; (b) ... must NOT provide for the remuneration or costs to be payable as a PERCENTAGE OR PROPORTION
-- of the amount of damages or other amounts awarded". (5): a term excluding negligence liability is void.
--
-- Singapore allows conditional fees (uplifts) in prescribed proceedings, and never contingency fees measured as a share of
-- what the client wins. The prescribed proceedings are in regulations, not retrieved.
DECLARE FeeArrangement IS ONE OF
    `ordinary hourly fees`
    `no win no fee with an uplift on success`
    `a percentage of the damages`
    `no win no fee with no uplift`

DECLARE FeeFacts HAS
    `the arrangement` IS A FeeArrangement
    `the proceedings are prescribed for conditional fees` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in writing and signed by the client` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A FeeFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the fee agreement is permitted` IF
    CONSIDER `the facts`'s `the arrangement`
    WHEN `ordinary hourly fees` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a percentage of the damages` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE `the facts`'s `the proceedings are prescribed for conditional fees` AND `the facts`'s `in writing and signed by the client`

§§ `118, 122 -- suing for fees and assessing the bill`

-- s 118(1): a solicitor must not sue for costs "until the expiry of ONE MONTH after he or she has delivered" a signed bill,
-- save with the court's permission (s 119: the client is about to leave Singapore, become bankrupt, and the like).
-- s 122: "After the expiry of 12 MONTHS from the delivery of a bill of costs, OR AFTER PAYMENT of the bill, no order is to
-- be made for assessment ..., except upon notice to the solicitor and under SPECIAL CIRCUMSTANCES".
--
-- A client who pays a bill they think excessive, meaning to challenge it later, has given up assessment as of course.
GIVEN `days since the bill was delivered` IS A NUMBER, `the court gave permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the solicitor may sue for the fees` IF
    `days since the bill was delivered` GREATER THAN 30 OR `the court gave permission`

GIVEN `months since delivery` IS A NUMBER, `the bill has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the client may have the bill assessed without special circumstances` IF
    `months since delivery` AT MOST 12 AND NOT `the bill has been paid`

§§ `83 -- discipline`

-- s 83(1): on due cause shown, an advocate and solicitor may be (a) struck off, (b) suspended "for a period not exceeding 5
-- years", (c) ordered to pay "a penalty of not more than $100,000", (d) censured, or (e) a penalty with (b) or (d).
-- (2): due cause includes (a) a conviction implying a defect of character; (b) fraudulent or grossly improper conduct, or
-- breach of the conduct rules amounting to improper conduct; (d) to (f) paying for or accepting touted work; (h)
-- "misconduct unbefitting an advocate and solicitor as an officer of the Supreme Court or as a member of an honourable
-- profession"; (i) carrying on a business incompatible with law; and (k) being disbarred, struck off, suspended, fined,
-- censured OR REPRIMANDED as a lawyer "in any other jurisdiction".
--
-- Limb (k) imports any foreign sanction, down to a reprimand, as due cause in Singapore.
DECLARE Cause IS ONE OF
    `a conviction implying a defect of character`
    `grossly improper conduct`
    `paying a tout`
    `misconduct unbefitting the profession`
    `an incompatible business`
    `a reprimand by a foreign bar`
    `losing a case`

GIVEN `the cause` IS A Cause
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the cause can be due cause for discipline` IF
    CONSIDER `the cause`
    WHEN `losing a case` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE Sanction HAS
    `struck off` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months of suspension` IS A NUMBER
    `penalty` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the sanction` IS A Sanction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sanction is within section 83(1)` IF
        `the sanction`'s `months of suspension` AT MOST 60
    AND `the sanction`'s `penalty` AT MOST 100000
